  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Airport Infrastructure Improvement Project (SEFF Activity 1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the first activity of the SEFF, ADB will finance (i) development of feasibility study for the construction of the proposed new Tbilisi international; (ii) social and environmental safeguards assessment; and (iii) capacity building activities for the executing and implementing agencies (EA/IA). The project was identified and proposed for further study as part of Georgia&amp;apos;s airport sector assessment conducted by ADB under the TA 6707-GEO. The new airport masterplan is currently being developed under the same TA. The proposed project is part of the government strategy to enhance Georgia&amp;apos;s connectivity and develop the country as an important regional transport and logistics hub. The project also aligns with the crosscutting priority of regional integration under ADB&amp;apos;s CPS 20242028. Inclusion of the project under the SEFF will ensure sufficient financing is allocated and the project is prepared for the construction phase if the feasibility is confirmed.</narrative>
  </description>
